    "SuiteTalk SOAP Web Services",
    "RESTlets (SuiteScript customer-specific)"
  ],
  "ScopeReason": "Operator-specified knowingly: SuiteTalk REST Web Services only — Record Service (CRUD on standard + custom record types) + SuiteQL query service. SuiteAnalytics Connect excluded (JDBC/ODBC protocol, not REST/JSON). SuiteTalk SOAP excluded (legacy XML, being deprecated — last endpoint 2025.2, disabled 2028.2). RESTlets excluded (customer-specific SuiteScript, no standard schema).",
  "SOAPDeprecationNote": "Oracle NetSuite is deprecating SuiteTalk SOAP Web Services. According to Oracle''s deprecation policy, the SOAP endpoint will be disabled in a future release (timeline: last endpoint supported through 2025.2, planned disablement 2028.2). The REST API Guide includes a ''SOAP Web Services To REST Web Services Upgrade Guide'' as the authoritative migration path. This connector targets the REST API exclusively. Source: SuiteTalk Web Services landing page (https://docs.oracle.com/en/cloud/saas/netsuite/ns-online-help/set_22152129.html) listing ''SOAP Web Services To Rest Web Services Upgrade Guide'' as a primary resource.",
  "TokenRefreshStrategy": "n/a-tba-does-not-expire",
  "TokenRefreshStrategyNote": "NetSuite TBA (OAuth 1.0a) tokens do NOT expire by default — they are long-lived until explicitly revoked by an administrator. The connector does not need to refresh tokens. If OAuth 2.0 is adopted as the auth method, standard OAuth 2.0 access token refresh applies (implementation needed at that time). Source: NetSuite TBA documentation implies persistent tokens (Access Token ID/Secret issued once and reused). EvidenceStrength: ImpliedFromExample.",
  "RecordsBodyFormat": "application/vnd.oracle.resource+json",
  "RecordsBodyFormatNote": "NetSuite REST uses custom media types for request/response bodies. The standard content type for record operations is ''application/vnd.oracle.resource+json'' with a type parameter: ''type=collection'' (list), ''type=singular'' (single record), ''type=create-form'', ''type=edit-form''. Standard ''application/json'' is used for error responses and SuiteQL bodies. Source: Working with OpenAPI 3.0 Metadata response excerpt showing content types; create-form operation showing Accept/Content-Type header values. https://docs.oracle.com/en/cloud/saas/netsuite/ns-online-help/article_1217103046.html",
  "SuiteQLRequiredHeader": "Prefer: transient",
  "SuiteQLRequiredHeaderNote": "SuiteQL POST requests MUST include the header ''Prefer: transient''. Without this header, the request will fail. Source: Executing SuiteQL Queries Through REST Web Services (https://docs.oracle.com/en/cloud/saas/netsuite/ns-online-help/section_157909186990.html): ''Note that Prefer: transient is a required header parameter.''",
  "RequestSizeLimit": "104MB",
  "RequestSizeLimitNote": "REST requests have a maximum size of 104MB. Source: REST Web Services Request Processing (https://docs.oracle.com/en/cloud/saas/netsuite/ns-online-help/chapter_161251386312.html): ''Note: REST requests have a size limit of 104MB.''",
  "SublistScopeExtension": {
    "decision": "Retain 2 representative sublist child IOs (InvoiceItem, SalesOrderItem) as Declared, read-only, graph-descended objects that sit OUTSIDE the 203-type Oracle authoritative REST catalog.",
    "authoritativeCatalogCount": 203,
    "emittedIOCount": 205,
